          "quote": "Use the one-stage map of [[def-rosenbrock-euler-step-map]] with the same $t,y,h,\\gamma,f$ but matrices $J$ and $\\widetilde J$. If $I_d-\\gamma hJ$ and $I_d-\\gamma h\\widetilde J$ are invertible, with inverse norms bounded by $K$ and $\\widetilde K$, then\n$$\\|\\Phi_{\\gamma,h}^{\\widetilde J}(t,y)-\\Phi_{\\gamma,h}^{J}(t,y)\\|_2\\le\\gamma h^2K\\widetilde K\\|\\widetilde J-J\\|_2\\,\\|f(t,y)\\|_2.$$\nThis is a one-step perturbation bound; it alone gives no uniform stability or convergence claim for a sequence of approximate Jacobians.",
