          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $d\\ge1$, $B\\in\\mathbb R^{d\\times d}$, $h>0$, $\\gamma>0$, and $0\\le q<1$ satisfy $\\|\\gamma hB\\|_2\\le q$, where $\\|\\cdot\\|_2$ is the matrix norm induced by the Euclidean vector $2$-norm, as in [[def-induced-matrix-p-norm]]. Then $A=I_d-\\gamma hB$ is invertible and\n$$\\|A^{-1}\\|_2\\le \\frac{1}{1-q}.$$\nIn particular, if $\\|\\gamma hB\\|_2\\le\\tfrac12$, then $\\|A^{-1}\\|_2\\le2$.",
