          "quote": "**Input:** a stored real square matrix $M\\in\\mathbb R^{d\\times d}$ with $d\\ge1$; a unit roundoff $u>0$ with $du<1$; and a terminating certificate evaluator `evaluator`. For each requested Euclidean or Frobenius norm of stored data, `evaluator` returns a finite stored nonnegative upper bound for the exact norm or `unavailable`. For each requested nonnegative expression formed from such upper bounds, $u$, and $d$, it returns a finite stored nonnegative upper bound for the exact expression or `unavailable`. Every returned bound is sound. All reflector, substitution, dot-product, and residual operations below use [[def-operationwise-real-complex-floating-point-model-with-sqrt-and-fma]]; certificate-evaluator calls return certified bounds rather than relying on ordinary rounded evaluation of a bound expression.\n\nDenote the top-level factor-only operation by `factor(M,u,evaluator)`. It returns either a reusable factor object or a factorization failure status.\n\n1. Set $R:=M$. For each column $j=0,\\ldots,d-1$, let $x$ be the active part of column $j$ of $R$ and $B$ the active trailing block to its right. Call [[alg-scaled-householder-reflector-formation-and-application]] on $(x,B)$. If it returns `range-failure`, return that status and no factor object. If it returns a marked `identity` or `reflector` result, replace the active block by its returned $C_+$, store its marker and (when present) $(v,\\widehat\\tau)$, and continue. For any other return, stop and return `factorization-failure` with no factor object. The resulting $R$ is upper triangular with its lower entries set to exact zeros by the called procedure; this is the full/reduced computational QR convention of [[def-full-reduced-and-column-pivoted-computational-qr-factorisations]].\n2. If any diagonal entry $R_{jj}$ is zero, return `singular-factor`. Otherwise return a factor object containing the original stored $M$, $R$, the ordered stored reflectors, $u$, and the certificate evaluator