          "id": "derivation-1-1",
          "claim": "Take a nonzero starting value $y$. The exact complex equations in the Statement give $hk_1/y=z/(1-\\alpha z)$ and, by $k_2=q_2+k_1$, the equivalent equation $(1-\\alpha z)k_2=F_1-\\alpha z k_1$. Substituting $F_1=\\lambda(y+hk_1/2)$ and eliminating $k_1$ yields $1+hk_2/y=1+[z+(1/2-2\\alpha)z^2]/(1-\\alpha z)^2$. Since $\\alpha=1-1/\\sqrt2$ satisfies $\\alpha^2+1/2-2\\alpha=0$, this reduces to the stated $R(z)$.",
