          "id": "derivation-2-1",
          "claim": "Let $z=x+iy$ with $x\\le0$. The equation $1-\\alpha z=0$ would force $z=1/\\alpha>0$, so the denominator has no zero in the closed left half-plane. Put $c=1-2\\alpha=\\sqrt2\\alpha$. Expanding gives $|1-\\alpha z|^4-|1+cz|^2=(-4\\alpha-2c)x+(2\\alpha^2-c^2)|z|^2+4\\alpha^2x^2-4\\alpha^3x|z|^2+\\alpha^4|z|^4=-2x+4\\alpha^2x^2-4\\alpha^3x|z|^2+\\alpha^4|z|^4\\ge0$. Every term is nonnegative because $x\\le0$ and $\\alpha>0$, so $|R(z)|\\le1$.",
