        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-rosenbrock-euler-local-defect-and-residual-error",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $D\\subseteq\\mathbb R\\times\\mathbb R^d$ be open and $f:D\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be $C^2$ (componentwise, as in [[def-ck-euclidean-maps-and-diffeomorphisms]]). Let $y(s)$ solve $y'=f(s,y)$ on $[t,t+h]$, $h>0$, and set $J=D_yf(t,y(t))$. Suppose the trajectory lies in a region where $\\|f\\|_2\\le F$, $\\|D_yf\\|_2\\le L$, and $\\|f_t+D_yf\\,f\\|_2\\le M_1$. Fix $\\gamma>0$ and a real matrix $\\widetilde J$. Suppose $A=I-\\gamma hJ$ and $\\widetilde A=I-\\gamma h\\widetilde J$ are invertible with $\\|A^{-1}\\|_2\\le\\kappa_0$ and $\\|\\widetilde A^{-1}\\|_2\\le\\kappa_1$. Write $\\delta=\\|\\widetilde J-J\\|_2$.\n\nFor the exact-arithmetic Rosenbrock stage map $\\Phi_{\\gamma,h}^{\\widetilde J}$, and a computed stage $\\widehat k$ whose update residual obeys $\\|\\widetilde A\\widehat k-f(t,y(t))\\|_2\\le\\rho$, the update $\\widehat y_+=y(t)+h\\widehat k$ satisfies\n$$\\|\\widehat y_+-y(t+h)\\|_2\\le C_Eh^2+\\kappa_1h\\rho, \\qquad C_E:=\\gamma\\kappa_0LF+\\frac{M_1}{2}+\\gamma\\kappa_0\\kappa_1\\delta F.$$\nThe last term is the separate Jacobian-approximation allowance. The residual is an equation residual in the units of [[def-implicit-residual-and-algebraic-error-units]], not a forward-error estimate by itself.",
