          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $f:U\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be autonomous and $C^1$ on an open $U\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$, let $y\\in U$, and let $h>0$. Suppose $I_d-hD f(y)$ is invertible. Then the exact-arithmetic Rosenbrock–Euler step with $\\gamma=1$ is the first Newton correction of the backward-Euler residual at the initial guess $y$. This does not assert that the corrected point solves the full backward-Euler equation.",
